# The writes and triggers a feat or a graft still makes on a table it does
# not own, one `<owner>: <what>` a line, each to move to its owner: a feat's
# rows change only through its own code, and a graft writes only its own
# schema, changing a feat by calling that feat's published write from its
# handler (_corpus/doc/architecture.md#writes-stay-home). `cella check
# feats` refuses a foreign write this list does not name, and a line whose
# write is gone, so the list only shrinks; nothing is added to it. Empty,
# it goes.
patronage-payslip: patronage_payslip.parts() writes patronage.part
patronage-payslip: trigger parts_by_pay on patronage.distribution
patronage-timesheet: patronage_timesheet.parts() writes patronage.part
patronage-timesheet: trigger parts_by_time on patronage.distribution
